## Step 2: Build Direct Skills ✅

Created 5 files under `src/lib/agent/skills/`:

### Project Structure

```
src/lib/agent/skills/
├── index.ts          # Skill registry — exports getActiveTools()
├── filesystem.ts     # read_file, write_file, list_directory, delete_file
├── terminal.ts       # execute_command (30s timeout)
├── web-search.ts     # web_search (DuckDuckGo HTML scraping)
└── download.ts       # download_file (curl as agent_worker)
```

### How sandboxing works

All file and terminal operations execute via:
```typescript
sudo -u agent_worker bash -c "<command>"
```

The OS kernel enforces that `agent_worker` can only access `/home/agent_worker/workspace`. Web search runs as the main user since it only makes network requests (no local file access).

### Skill Registry

Tools are organized into **Skills** — groups of related tools. The `core` skill is always active:

```typescript
const coreSkill: Skill = {
    name: "core",
    tools: [...filesystemTools, ...terminalTools, ...webSearchTools, ...downloadTools],
    alwaysActive: true,
};
```

Future skills can be added and toggled per session.

